  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "In triangle \\(ABC,\\) \\(AC=24\\) inches, \\(BC=10\\) inches, \\(AB=26\\) inches. The radius of the inscribed circle is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(26\\) in"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(4\\) in"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(13\\) in"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(8\\) in"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "None of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "4"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p35.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(10^2+24^2=26^2,\\) the triangle is right. Its area is \\(\\tfrac12(10)(24)=120,\\) and its semiperimeter is \\(\\tfrac{10+24+26}{2}=30.\\) Using \\(K=rs,\\) the inradius, in inches, is \\[ r=\\frac{K}{s}=\\frac{120}{30}=4. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "The side lengths form a right triangle",
        "For a right triangle with legs \\(a,b\\) and hypotenuse \\(c,\\) the inradius is \\(\\frac{a+b-c}{2}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
